1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:01,680
(Are you sure you can be alone?)

2
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:03,120
(I’ll be fine, Pa.)

3
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:05,240
Surprise!

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,280
(Bay and I have been seeing each other for a while.)

5
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,200
- Can you come with me?
-To where?

6
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:15,280
If this doesn’t work,

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,040
you won’t have to see me again.

8
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:20,800
I’m begging you.

9
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:24,280
Can you let me live like a normal kid for a night?

10
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:27,080
Just don’t come home too late.

11
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:57,880
- What time is it now?
- What time is it?

12
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:00,480
10.59. Yes!

13
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:10,720
I said come home by 11 but you didn’t
have to wait until the last second.

14
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:18,800
Where are you staying tonight, Bay?

15
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:20,960
Uhh...

16
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:25,400
I can stay at my friend’s place, sir.

17
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:30,760
It’s late.

18
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:34,280
You can sleep with Sun tonight.

19
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:40,440
Pa!

20
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:44,360
Thank you, Pa.

21
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:50,840
Thank you so much…Pa.

22
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:57,800
I’m going to bed now.

23
00:01:58,560 --> 00:01:59,680
Lock up for me.

24
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:04,600
Yes.

25
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:12,000
Are you crazy? My dad could see that.

26
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:13,560
Oh, he didn’t.

27
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:24,600
Just get in.

28
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:26,960
We’ll figure it out tomorrow.

29
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:48,240
Hey!

30
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,200
You’re taking the blanket all by yourself?

31
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:54,000
Fine, I’ll get another one.

32
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:55,840
Hey, don’t.

33
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,120
Use this one.

34
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:00,440
We can share it.

35
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:02,600
If you’re cold,

36
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:03,960
you can spoon me.

37
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:15,400
If you’re not cold, that’s fine.

38
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:19,000
But I am. So…let me spoon you.

39
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:43,600
Just like that?

40
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:11,800
(SAMING PHON FAI)

41
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:22,560
(SUPPORTED BY THE DEPARTMENT OF CULTURAL PROMOTION, MINISTRY OF CULTURE)

42
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:34,240
(SAMING PHON FAI)

43
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:39,280
Ooh.

44
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:44,080
Pa’s famous Stir-fried Morning Glory.

45
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:46,520
- I can’t wait to try it.
- Eat up.

46
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:47,680
-I will.
-There’s omelet, too.

47
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:52,200
Here you go, boys.

48
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:53,720
Wow, Pa!

49
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:55,800
Are you feeding the whole block?

50
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:58,960
Well, I wasn’t sure how much I should make.

51
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:01,440
I’ve been living and eating alone lately.

52
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:03,040
Now there are two more people.

53
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:05,440
And you teenage boys must eat a lot, right?

54
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:08,960
That’s true, Pa. I always eat a lot when I’m home.

55
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:10,800
See? Bay loves to eat.

56
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:13,440
Come on. Let’s eat when it’s still hot.

57
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:15,520
- Here, Pa.
- Come on.

58
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:18,040
- Thank you, sir.
- Eat up, boy.

59
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:21,320
-Eat more.
-Pa, he gets more rice than I do.

60
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:24,640
- Here you go.
- Thank you, Pa.

61
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:26,840
Dig in, boys.

62
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:40,160
Hmm!

63
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:42,360
So delicious, Pa!

64
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,120
See?

65
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:46,440
- This is delicious.
- Good. Eat it up then.

66
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:50,640
I bet Bee doesn’t feed you this well.

67
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:59,120
Hey, Sun. The tryout for the national team
starts tomorrow, right?

68
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:00,880
Really?

69
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,800
- I’ll be there to support you then.
- Oh, please. There are four rounds.

70
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:07,360
You can come for the final round.

71
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:09,360
I’m sure I can make it.

72
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:11,600
Alright, Golden Boy.

73
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:16,320
But now you have to train and compete in the tryout, too.

74
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:19,560
Do you want to stay at the dorm instead?
Should be easier.

75
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:23,760
If that’s okay with you.

76
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:26,600
Staying at the dorm would be more convenient.

77
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:29,640
And I’ll come home on the weekends.

78
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:32,920
- Is that okay, Pa?
- Sure. I’m fine with that.

79
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:34,480
What about you, Bay?

80
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:45,480
If you’re still figuring it out,

81
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:47,560
you can stay with me.

82
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:50,160
- Right, Pa?
- Oh?

83
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,080
Let Bay stay with us.

84
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,000
What’s on your mind?

85
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:27,880
My stomach is burning.

86
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:29,560
Huh?

87
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:31,680
You guys have only fed me spicy food.

88
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:33,520
I usually eat something mild.

89
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:34,840
Like...

90
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:37,160
tofu and stuff.

91
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:44,320
But…don’t you miss your home?

92
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:45,520
I do.

93
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:48,600
I’m thinking about…

94
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:51,960
what I left at my house.

95
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:56,160
What…do you mean?

96
00:08:57,520 --> 00:09:00,320
I left my computer,

97
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:02,280
my clothes,

98
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:05,400
- and some documents for my portfolio.
- Wait, wait ,wait.

99
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:07,480
Don’t you miss your dad at all?

100
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:08,240
Nah.

101
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:11,000
All I think about is…

102
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:15,480
how I will get my stuff without getting caught.

103
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:08,320
Where are you taking all this?!

104
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:10,560
Bay!

105
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:15,240
If you walk away, don’t ever come back again, you brat!

106
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:26,040
You stop seeing that boy right now!

107
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:28,720
Or else, don’t bother coming back here!

108
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:30,360
And I’m cutting you off, too!

109
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:33,040
If you’re so tough, get a job and feed yourself

110
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:38,080
Bee, can you get it together, huh?

111
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:39,560
Shut the f*ck up, Chun!

112
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:42,320
Your son has a bad influence on my son, bastard!

113
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:46,120
- Hey, hey, hey. Don’t talk about my son!
- Pa. Pa.

114
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:46,920
Come on!

115
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,320
Pa, enough.

116
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:51,760
Pa, get in the house.

117
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:53,560
Come on and finish this, Chun!

118
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:54,960
Are you a coward?

119
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:56,520
You can’t face me, coward?!

120
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:07,520
You pick up all his junk!

121
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:14,200
Take this, too!

122
00:11:22,160 --> 00:11:23,280
You take it all!

123
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:25,920
Brats!

124
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:12,440
Don’t you want to call your mom at least?

125
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:18,880
She must be busy taking care of my grandma.

126
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:21,800
She wouldn’t want to hear about this thing.

127
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:24,280
But this is not just something Bay.

128
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:26,840
This is a big deal.

129
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:31,320
I don’t want other people to worry about me.

130
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:40,640
Don’t say that, Bay.

131
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:47,680
No matter what it is,

132
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:51,480
you can talk to me about it.

133
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:02,400
You don’t have to carry this on your shoulders, Bay.

134
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:06,960
I’m here for you, always.

135
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:14,840
Or should we call Boat instead?

136
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:18,600
Boat must be busy right now.

137
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:24,640
It’s okay.

138
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:28,560
I’ll call him myself.

139
00:13:41,160 --> 00:13:41,800
Hello.

140
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:43,280
Hello, Boat.

141
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:45,160
This is Sun.

142
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:48,160
Yeah. What’s going on?

143
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:49,280
Is there something wrong?

144
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:54,600
Well...

145
00:13:59,200 --> 00:14:01,280
Bay is having trouble with his dad.

146
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:07,960
Why? What happened?

147
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:18,600
Why didn’t you call me?

148
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:20,920
Mom!

149
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:42,840
I left you guys alone for a few months.
What happened to this family, huh?

150
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:47,200
Boat,

151
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:50,040
why didn’t you tell me about all of this?

152
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:54,280
And you are no better.

153
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:57,480
Whenever I called to check on you guys,
you said everything’s fine.

154
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:58,920
Does this look fine to you?

155
00:15:00,240 --> 00:15:03,520
It’s these two who ruined our family’s reputation.

156
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:07,760
Isn’t it because you made Boat lie about being an intern

157
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:10,800
- just so you could brag about it to Sun’s family?
- Bay!

158
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:14,520
And you wouldn’t even let me and Sun be friends

159
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:17,600
because you just couldn’t get out of your stupid way!

160
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:20,200
- Bay, don’t you speak to me that way!
- Why can’t I?

161
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:23,360
Why would you drag us all into this?
Why, Dad?

162
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:27,120
Do you even realize that this is all your fault?

163
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:30,040
Bay, it’s not your dad’s fault.

164
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:34,320
I don’t know if he stole their recipe or not, Mom.

165
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:36,960
But opening a dim sum shop across from his place,

166
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:38,240
someone he used to call friend.

167
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:40,600
What kind of person does that?!

168
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:43,640
If you don’t know anything, shut
your mouth, Bay!

169
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:48,400
You don’t know what I had to do to take care of this family!

170
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:49,960
But using your own struggles

171
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:52,040
as an excuse to treat their family badly…

172
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:53,480
Do you think that’s right, Dad?!

173
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:56,920
Don’t you walk away, Bay.
Come back and apologize to me!

174
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:58,920
- Bay!!
- Bay, come back!

175
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:00,200
Bay!

176
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:03,360
Bay!

177
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:05,240
Bay, come back!

178
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:07,320
Bay!

179
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:09,200
Bay!

180
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:13,160
- Bay! Bay, don’t go!
- Mom, mom. I’ll go after him. Don’t worry.

181
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:40,080
Thank you so much, Coach,

182
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:43,280
for telling us Bay was here.

183
00:16:58,960 --> 00:16:59,320
Hey.

184
00:17:19,360 --> 00:17:20,120
I’m sorry

185
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:25,560
for not picking up the phone.

186
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:28,840
It’s okay.

187
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:33,760
For earlier,

188
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,240
I want to apologize, too.

189
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:40,280
About what?

190
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:44,000
I don’t know.

191
00:17:46,280 --> 00:17:48,600
Whenever Dad tried to guilt trip you,

192
00:17:51,520 --> 00:17:53,080
I wasn’t able to defend you.

193
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:02,920
Now I really know how it feels

194
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:08,040
to be hated by my own father.

195
00:18:23,880 --> 00:18:26,040
I’d like to properly thank you

196
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:28,240
for taking care of Bay.

197
00:18:29,040 --> 00:18:30,920
It’s nothing. Don’t worry about it.

198
00:18:34,520 --> 00:18:35,080
Mom.

199
00:18:39,560 --> 00:18:40,800
- Bay.
- Mom.

200
00:18:46,720 --> 00:18:47,560
Where have you been?

201
00:18:51,120 --> 00:18:52,280
I’m so sorry, Mom.

202
00:18:53,520 --> 00:18:57,520
I’m sorry, too, for not knowing about this sooner.

203
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:05,200
Bay, do you want to stay with me at Grandma’s?

204
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:09,880
I’d like to stay with Sun, Mom.

205
00:19:23,640 --> 00:19:24,560
That’s fine.

206
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,120
But don’t forget to call me, okay?

207
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:30,680
I will, Mom.

208
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:27,560
(Call me or Boat if you need anything?)

209
00:21:00,360 --> 00:21:01,360
What are you doing?

210
00:21:05,240 --> 00:21:05,960
And where did you get this?

211
00:21:07,920 --> 00:21:09,000
I stole it from our prom night.

212
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:11,120
Thought it was kinda cute.

213
00:21:12,320 --> 00:21:12,800
I liked it.

214
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:19,280
I just didn’t know how to cheer you up.

215
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:32,560
Why are you so cute?

216
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:39,280
Just staying by my side

217
00:21:40,080 --> 00:21:41,680
and being cute like this is enough.

218
00:21:45,040 --> 00:21:46,360
Or you can take your shirt off.

219
00:21:47,240 --> 00:21:48,840
-I like it when you’re half naked.
-You perv.

220
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,000
Hey, I thought you wanted to cheer me up.

221
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:54,240
No, I’m done.

222
00:21:56,280 --> 00:21:58,680
Hey, your boyfriend is feeling down.

223
00:22:13,280 --> 00:22:16,040
Hey, what was that? I didn’t see it.

224
00:22:16,680 --> 00:22:20,080
-Let me see. Please, I’d like to see more.
-Haven’t you seen enough already?

225
00:22:20,280 --> 00:22:22,560
-Let me see. I wanna see.
-That’s enough.

226
00:22:23,120 --> 00:22:24,520
Let me see.

227
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:30,920
Let’s go.

228
00:22:32,320 --> 00:22:33,320
I’m off to school, Dad.

229
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:35,400
-See you.
-See you.

230
00:22:37,040 --> 00:22:38,160
I’ll meet you at the dorm, okay?

231
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:41,040
I’m off. Bye-bye.

232
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:01,920
Pa.

233
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:08,120
Seeing their family fight because Bay and I are together,

234
00:23:09,840 --> 00:23:13,160
I can’t help but feel guilty, Pa.

235
00:23:25,120 --> 00:23:26,920
Now that your dad’s cut you off,

236
00:23:27,520 --> 00:23:29,320
will he pay for your tuition in Italy?

237
00:23:29,840 --> 00:23:30,160
No.

238
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:34,280
But I’d still like to see if I’m qualified.

239
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:36,960
If I am, that means one day

240
00:23:37,960 --> 00:23:39,800
I might figure out how to get there on my own.

241
00:23:43,640 --> 00:23:45,200
-Hello
-Hello

242
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:47,160
-Morning, guys.
-Good morning.

243
00:23:47,440 --> 00:23:48,640
Hi, Bay. Hi, Petong.

244
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:50,040
How are you holding up, Bay?

245
00:23:51,520 --> 00:23:52,920
I haven’t told you anything.

246
00:23:53,600 --> 00:23:55,200
Everyone on Discord knows what happened.

247
00:23:57,480 --> 00:23:58,640
Are you okay now?

248
00:23:59,240 --> 00:24:00,960
Mmm, I’m okay, I guess.

249
00:24:02,160 --> 00:24:05,320
-Not okay. This is not okay.
-We’re here for you, okay?

250
00:24:13,760 --> 00:24:16,200
Bay-Sun fandom is here for you as well.

251
00:24:18,240 --> 00:24:18,880
Nice.

252
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:22,280
And your fans got you something.

253
00:24:23,040 --> 00:24:26,520
Over there, that’s your food support.

254
00:24:26,840 --> 00:24:29,840
Wow! You’ve got lots of support, huh?

255
00:24:29,880 --> 00:24:31,440
You can take it all home, Bay.

256
00:24:31,640 --> 00:24:32,840
Okay, okay.

257
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:34,440
I call dips on orange cake.

258
00:24:35,360 --> 00:24:35,960
It’s all mine.

259
00:24:36,720 --> 00:24:39,240
-Don’t eat it all by yourself.
-Let me have some. Come on

260
00:24:39,800 --> 00:24:40,480
Fine.

261
00:24:43,880 --> 00:24:46,800
Thanks a lot for keeping an eye on Bay.

262
00:24:47,800 --> 00:24:49,560
Oh, that’s not a big deal.

263
00:24:50,160 --> 00:24:53,720
Just seeing Bay and Sun together makes me really happy.

264
00:24:54,720 --> 00:24:57,040
The only problem now is your dad.

265
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:04,880
Oh, no.

266
00:25:05,520 --> 00:25:07,120
-Hey, are you alright?
-My bad.

267
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:09,760
-Hey.
-Whoa, whoa, whoa.

268
00:25:10,840 --> 00:25:12,080
I’m so so sorry.

269
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:12,840
It’s fine.

270
00:25:29,440 --> 00:25:30,200
Are you okay?

271
00:25:32,920 --> 00:25:33,520
I’m okay.

272
00:25:34,120 --> 00:25:35,200
I should ask you if you’re okay.

273
00:25:35,720 --> 00:25:38,200
You were quite absent-minded.

274
00:25:39,600 --> 00:25:40,520
Nothing. I was just…

275
00:25:42,560 --> 00:25:43,760
thinking about the past.

276
00:25:48,960 --> 00:25:49,880
You remember Ming?

277
00:25:51,720 --> 00:25:52,320
Ming…

278
00:25:54,160 --> 00:25:55,800
Sun’s brother? Why?

279
00:25:59,680 --> 00:26:01,040
We were so close back then.

280
00:26:03,240 --> 00:26:04,560
But since our fathers had a fight,

281
00:26:07,320 --> 00:26:09,640
we’ve never looked at each other again.

282
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:17,560
I pushed myself so hard to get into medical school.

283
00:26:19,600 --> 00:26:20,960
So my dad could brag about it to their family.

284
00:26:22,440 --> 00:26:23,840
But did that change anything?

285
00:26:27,840 --> 00:26:28,440
It didn’t.

286
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:33,920
I do love my dad.

287
00:26:41,320 --> 00:26:44,040
But it’s so hard to live with him.

288
00:26:47,120 --> 00:26:49,520
Can I ask you something?

289
00:26:53,920 --> 00:26:54,480
What?

290
00:26:57,000 --> 00:26:58,400
Can I give you a hug?

291
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:04,360
Thank you.

292
00:27:15,400 --> 00:27:17,720
Boat, you did your best, okay?

293
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:23,760
Thank you.

294
00:27:34,080 --> 00:27:36,600
Today is the first round of the qualifiers.

295
00:27:36,760 --> 00:27:38,680
We’ll go from 32 players down to 16.

296
00:27:39,120 --> 00:27:41,440
The winner of each match will advance

297
00:27:41,840 --> 00:27:45,480
and return for the second round next Thursday.

298
00:27:45,840 --> 00:27:47,400
It’s a single-elimination format,

299
00:27:47,760 --> 00:27:50,680
with the final round taking place on February 20.

300
00:27:50,680 --> 00:27:51,080
FEBRUARY 2026

301
00:27:51,160 --> 00:27:53,320
We’re selecting five players to represent the Thai national team,

302
00:27:53,560 --> 00:27:54,720
along with three reserve players.

303
00:27:54,920 --> 00:27:55,560
Understand?
Yes.

304
00:28:09,560 --> 00:28:10,080
Bay,

305
00:28:11,320 --> 00:28:14,200
Next week, after Chinese New Year, the national team tryouts.

306
00:28:14,720 --> 00:28:15,120
Hey!

307
00:28:16,440 --> 00:28:17,840
My boyfriend is going national now?

308
00:28:20,720 --> 00:28:21,600
And after Chinese New Year,

309
00:28:22,640 --> 00:28:23,520
I think I’m going home.

310
00:28:24,960 --> 00:28:25,720
Wanna come with me?

311
00:28:33,440 --> 00:28:34,680
Don’t look sad.

312
00:28:37,840 --> 00:28:39,080
You can stay with me,

313
00:28:39,800 --> 00:28:40,720
so you won’t be lonely.

314
00:28:43,800 --> 00:28:44,520
Peek-a-boo!

315
00:28:45,560 --> 00:28:47,200
Well? Are you coming now?

316
00:28:54,440 --> 00:28:56,640
Alright, alright. I’m coming.

317
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:57,680
Five seconds.

318
00:28:58,200 --> 00:28:59,160
Just five?

319
00:28:59,840 --> 00:29:00,880
-Ten seconds.
-Five!

320
00:29:01,080 --> 00:29:01,880
-Eight!
-Six!

321
00:29:02,120 --> 00:29:03,800
-Seven?
-Six, final offer.

322
00:29:05,800 --> 00:29:06,280
Deal.

323
00:29:07,880 --> 00:29:08,960
-Deal.
-Deal.

324
00:29:09,800 --> 00:29:10,320
Ready?

325
00:29:14,040 --> 00:29:14,880
You sure?

326
00:29:17,960 --> 00:29:21,320
-One, two, three, four, five, six.
-Hey! That was too fast!

327
00:29:22,200 --> 00:29:24,280
Hey, open up!

328
00:29:33,640 --> 00:29:35,320
Are you challenging me?

329
00:29:42,200 --> 00:29:43,080
SAMING PHON FAI

330
00:29:43,120 --> 00:29:44,400
-Pa!
-Wacth out!

331
00:29:54,960 --> 00:29:55,800
That was loud.

332
00:29:59,440 --> 00:30:02,000
Guys, come on and eat. Come on.

333
00:30:02,720 --> 00:30:03,800
Come on, come on.

334
00:30:06,520 --> 00:30:07,760
That was loud.

335
00:30:11,320 --> 00:30:15,680
CLOSE DURING CHINESE NEW YEAR
FEBRUARY 17-19

336
00:30:32,960 --> 00:30:33,800
Are you okay?

337
00:30:37,760 --> 00:30:40,040
I thought I’d moved on.

338
00:30:41,480 --> 00:30:45,680
But seeing my house being so quiet like this…kinda makes me sad.

339
00:30:47,440 --> 00:30:48,160
I get it.

340
00:30:54,560 --> 00:30:57,680
Do you think my dad will ever accept us?

341
00:31:00,600 --> 00:31:01,880
Maybe one day he will.

342
00:31:02,920 --> 00:31:06,640
Look at my dad. Even he could come around and accept you.

343
00:31:09,560 --> 00:31:13,320
Seeing their family fight because
Bay and I are together,

344
00:31:15,120 --> 00:31:18,520
I can’t help but feel guilty, Pa.

345
00:31:20,320 --> 00:31:21,000
Sun,

346
00:31:23,120 --> 00:31:24,640
this is not your fault.

347
00:31:25,880 --> 00:31:27,680
It’s my fault and Bee’s fault.

348
00:31:31,600 --> 00:31:32,880
Even if you boys broke up,

349
00:31:33,560 --> 00:31:35,800
it wouldn’t make us stop fighting.

350
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:38,880
You’ve seen this before,

351
00:31:40,080 --> 00:31:41,640
with Ming and Boat.

352
00:31:42,240 --> 00:31:43,480
They stopped being friends

353
00:31:43,880 --> 00:31:45,120
and wouldn’t even look at each other.

354
00:31:45,920 --> 00:31:47,400
But that didn’t make anything better.

355
00:31:48,280 --> 00:31:48,800
Pa.

356
00:31:51,160 --> 00:31:52,200
I’m so sorry

357
00:31:53,800 --> 00:31:59,560
that it took me this long to realize
how badly Bee and I hurt all of you.

358
00:32:05,600 --> 00:32:09,720
I guess it will take Bee some time
to realize it, too.

359
00:32:11,640 --> 00:32:13,600
I should know. It took me long enough.

360
00:32:20,840 --> 00:32:25,560
I think people in their 50s
still have their own coming-of-age moments.

361
00:32:27,720 --> 00:32:28,920
Hopefully, he’ll come around.

362
00:32:30,560 --> 00:32:31,480
Are you hungry?

363
00:32:31,920 --> 00:32:32,960
Wanna eat with us?

364
00:32:33,880 --> 00:32:34,720
Are you sure?

365
00:32:36,280 --> 00:32:37,040
Come on.

366
00:32:37,880 --> 00:32:39,440
Pa has prepared a huge feast.

367
00:32:40,800 --> 00:32:43,240
There are like 5-6 menus.

368
00:32:44,480 --> 00:32:46,560
So many dishes. Eat a lot, guys.

369
00:32:49,240 --> 00:32:50,440
We’re here.

370
00:32:50,640 --> 00:32:53,800
Oh, Sun. Come on and eat, boys.

371
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:54,880
Nice to meet you.

372
00:32:56,600 --> 00:32:58,840
And who is this boy?

373
00:33:00,600 --> 00:33:02,080
This is Bay.

374
00:33:03,640 --> 00:33:04,520
Bay?

375
00:33:07,680 --> 00:33:10,280
Is he the son of the man you had a problem with?

376
00:33:11,840 --> 00:33:12,240
Yes.

377
00:33:17,040 --> 00:33:17,920
But now…

378
00:33:19,440 --> 00:33:21,280
Bay and Sun are boyfriends.

379
00:33:29,600 --> 00:33:30,200
Bay.

380
00:33:30,840 --> 00:33:31,480
Yes, ma’am?

381
00:33:32,120 --> 00:33:34,080
You must have done something right.

382
00:33:35,240 --> 00:33:39,240
Even us, Chun’s siblings couldn’t do it.

383
00:33:40,040 --> 00:33:43,920
We’ve been trying to get him to let go of...

384
00:33:45,320 --> 00:33:47,120
the whole stealing-recipe thing for a long time.

385
00:33:48,400 --> 00:33:50,520
But this one never listened.

386
00:33:52,400 --> 00:33:57,720
You two did a great job getting him
to change his mind.

387
00:33:59,400 --> 00:34:03,080
Now Chun is like a different person.

388
00:34:05,520 --> 00:34:06,400
Great job, boys.

389
00:34:14,320 --> 00:34:14,960
For you.

390
00:34:16,560 --> 00:34:17,440
Thank you.

391
00:34:20,680 --> 00:34:21,640
You get one, too.

392
00:34:25,280 --> 00:34:26,240
Thank you, ma’am.

393
00:34:33,160 --> 00:34:34,240
Now let’s eat, guys.

394
00:34:34,360 --> 00:34:35,720
-Come on, boys.
-Let us eat.

395
00:34:36,120 --> 00:34:37,760
-So many dishes.
-Let’s dig in.

396
00:34:38,840 --> 00:34:39,240
Ma!

397
00:34:46,560 --> 00:34:48,160
Pa, hello.

398
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:51,960
Didn’t know you guys were coming.

399
00:34:52,840 --> 00:34:54,240
Sun called and invited us.

400
00:34:55,040 --> 00:34:55,880
Are you okay with that?

401
00:34:56,960 --> 00:34:57,680
Yes, of course.

402
00:35:00,440 --> 00:35:01,360
Come have a seat.

403
00:35:02,800 --> 00:35:04,360
-Good to see you.
-Come and sit.

404
00:35:04,560 --> 00:35:05,200
Hello, everyone.
-Nice to see you.
-Nice to see you.

405
00:35:05,800 --> 00:35:06,960
-Hello. Hello.
-Hello. Have a seat.

406
00:35:08,120 --> 00:35:09,200
I guess…

407
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:11,440
we’re gonna need more food.

408
00:35:13,200 --> 00:35:15,680
-Come on. Come help me in the kitchen.
-Oh, sure.

409
00:35:15,720 --> 00:35:16,960
-Let’s go.
-We’ll be back.

410
00:35:17,000 --> 00:35:19,440
-You guys eat. I’ll be right back.
-Yes, thank you.

411
00:35:21,600 --> 00:35:24,160
-Make a lot more, Auntie.
-Alright.

412
00:35:24,640 --> 00:35:25,440
This isn’t enough.

413
00:35:25,760 --> 00:35:26,480
Let’s get the rice.

414
00:35:26,880 --> 00:35:29,000
Try this, my aunt’s duck recipe.

415
00:35:37,320 --> 00:35:37,800
So good.

416
00:35:37,880 --> 00:35:39,280
-You like it?
-Yeah, it’s good.

417
00:35:39,880 --> 00:35:40,800
Told you.

418
00:35:41,320 --> 00:35:42,600
-You have some, too.
-Okay.

419
00:35:42,960 --> 00:35:43,720
Here you go.

420
00:35:45,600 --> 00:35:46,400
Thank you.

421
00:35:50,360 --> 00:35:50,920
Hmmm.

422
00:35:51,080 --> 00:35:53,120
A big piece of chicken. This is for you.

423
00:35:56,840 --> 00:35:59,440
Papa, have some Hoi Jo.

424
00:36:10,720 --> 00:36:11,800
Good evening.

425
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:22,520
Bay.

426
00:36:28,040 --> 00:36:28,680
Mom.

427
00:36:31,280 --> 00:36:31,760
SAMING PHON FAI
OPEN DAILY

428
00:36:31,800 --> 00:36:33,640
I bought you some Pad Mee, here.

429
00:36:34,200 --> 00:36:35,000
Thank you.

430
00:36:35,800 --> 00:36:36,600
Eat up.

431
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:40,920
Coach Kong, what are you doing here?

432
00:36:43,200 --> 00:36:45,400
I go where the food goes.

433
00:36:48,360 --> 00:36:49,560
As good as always.

434
00:37:00,440 --> 00:37:01,080
Go talk to him.

435
00:37:23,560 --> 00:37:24,080
Ming.

436
00:37:25,600 --> 00:37:26,560
Go talk to Boat.

437
00:37:27,640 --> 00:37:29,000
I have to speak with your dad.

438
00:37:45,760 --> 00:37:46,080
Sun.
Yes?

439
00:37:47,160 --> 00:37:47,840
Can I ask you something?

440
00:37:49,200 --> 00:37:51,400
Boat and Ming… What are they?

441
00:37:53,160 --> 00:37:55,640
Hmm, what do you mean?

442
00:37:57,040 --> 00:37:58,080
I mean...

443
00:38:00,400 --> 00:38:02,040
Are they like you and Bay?

444
00:38:03,440 --> 00:38:06,160
Are they fighting but actually liking each other?

445
00:38:07,080 --> 00:38:08,200
How would I know?

446
00:38:09,240 --> 00:38:11,080
If you want to know, you should go find out.

447
00:38:12,080 --> 00:38:14,920
If they seem to have feelings for each other,
you shut it down.

448
00:38:15,360 --> 00:38:15,760
Period.

449
00:38:16,360 --> 00:38:16,960
You’re right.

450
00:38:17,400 --> 00:38:19,400
I should have thought of that. I’ll be back.

451
00:38:19,400 --> 00:38:20,240
Are you insane?

452
00:38:21,040 --> 00:38:22,040
Just go, Coach.

453
00:38:23,280 --> 00:38:25,280
Don’t waste your time talking about it. Go.

454
00:38:26,400 --> 00:38:28,080
-Just go.
-I’m eating.

455
00:38:28,080 --> 00:38:28,960
Go, Coach, go.

456
00:38:39,680 --> 00:38:41,920
How’ve you been? Are you doing okay?

457
00:38:44,560 --> 00:38:46,320
Mmm, I’m doing fine.

458
00:38:52,120 --> 00:38:54,040
How long has it been since we talked
to each other?

459
00:38:56,480 --> 00:38:58,560
I didn’t even know how you were doing.

460
00:39:02,240 --> 00:39:03,480
Of course you didn’t.

461
00:39:04,600 --> 00:39:06,200
Look at what our dads have done.

462
00:39:09,000 --> 00:39:09,720
Anyway…

463
00:39:13,160 --> 00:39:13,920
I’m sorry.

464
00:39:17,600 --> 00:39:19,000
I shouldn’t have listened to my dad.

465
00:39:19,840 --> 00:39:23,960
I was your best friend but I didn’t do anything about it.

466
00:39:25,800 --> 00:39:27,560
I still regret it to this day.

467
00:39:32,400 --> 00:39:33,360
You don’t have to.

468
00:39:36,520 --> 00:39:38,800
You and I can still become friends again.

469
00:39:46,560 --> 00:39:47,360
I’m sorry, man.

470
00:39:47,960 --> 00:39:48,720
Ahem!

471
00:39:52,000 --> 00:39:53,680
What? Can’t I hug him?

472
00:39:53,800 --> 00:39:55,120
It was a friendly hug.

473
00:39:55,680 --> 00:39:59,120
I didn’t say anything, okay?
It was just a friendly, very friendly hug.

474
00:39:59,240 --> 00:40:00,360
We’re friends, see?

475
00:40:08,320 --> 00:40:10,200
Do whatever you want with your friend.

476
00:40:16,280 --> 00:40:20,080
Kong, Boat, wait for me in the car.
I need a minute.

477
00:40:20,520 --> 00:40:21,360
Okay, Mom.

478
00:40:33,520 --> 00:40:34,040
Honey.

479
00:40:35,120 --> 00:40:35,640
Honey.

480
00:40:36,520 --> 00:40:37,360
Wait.

481
00:40:43,040 --> 00:40:44,240
Just apologize to your sons.

482
00:40:47,320 --> 00:40:48,600
You want me to apologize?

483
00:40:50,040 --> 00:40:52,920
You know what I’ve done for this family.

484
00:40:53,840 --> 00:40:55,640
Have they ever appreciated their father?

485
00:40:55,640 --> 00:40:57,560
Stop using that as an excuse.

486
00:41:01,680 --> 00:41:02,480
It was my fault.

487
00:41:04,800 --> 00:41:05,680
You should blame me.

488
00:41:08,240 --> 00:41:09,000
I’m sorry.

489
00:41:23,960 --> 00:41:25,240
-Mom.
-Hmm?

490
00:41:27,040 --> 00:41:28,360
I already know the truth

491
00:41:31,680 --> 00:41:33,880
about our family stealing Chun’s dim sum recipe.

492
00:41:38,920 --> 00:41:41,920
I’ve never tasted Chun’s dim sum before.

493
00:41:44,800 --> 00:41:46,560
I knew right away when I tasted it.

494
00:41:58,200 --> 00:42:00,480
It tasted so similar to dad’s.

495
00:42:02,400 --> 00:42:03,920
Too similar.

496
00:42:42,920 --> 00:42:45,680
It was my fault we were in debt.

497
00:42:47,760 --> 00:42:50,120
I pressured you so much that you had to do such a thing .

498
00:42:51,280 --> 00:42:53,040
Okay, hold on a second.

499
00:42:53,040 --> 00:42:53,640
SAMING PHON FAI

500
00:42:53,720 --> 00:42:55,360
Hurry. Come help me, quick.

501
00:42:55,840 --> 00:42:58,400
Here, thank you so much.

502
00:43:00,880 --> 00:43:04,800
Here, two pork buns and two cream buns. Thank you.

503
00:43:05,160 --> 00:43:07,560
I’ll have one mantou and one BBQ pork bun, please.

504
00:43:07,560 --> 00:43:11,080
-Okay. You, make more. We’re almost out.
-Yes, sir.

505
00:43:12,200 --> 00:43:13,160
What was your order again?

506
00:43:37,920 --> 00:43:38,520
Honey.

507
00:43:42,760 --> 00:43:46,920
MORTGAGES ACCEPTED FOR HOUSES AND LAND

508
00:43:47,040 --> 00:43:48,080
We’ll get through this.

509
00:43:49,880 --> 00:43:51,600
It was all my fault.

510
00:43:52,360 --> 00:43:54,800
I let you do that to your friend.

511
00:43:55,640 --> 00:43:57,000
I could have stopped you

512
00:43:57,800 --> 00:43:59,040
but I didn’t do anything.

513
00:43:59,080 --> 00:44:00,880
-We didn’t do anything wrong.
-I let all this happen.

514
00:44:02,880 --> 00:44:04,160
None of us did anything wrong.

515
00:44:07,880 --> 00:44:09,840
I didn’t take Chun’s recipe

516
00:44:10,120 --> 00:44:11,760
and you don’t have to feel guilty.

517
00:44:14,280 --> 00:44:15,680
-Bee.
-Damn.

518
00:44:15,880 --> 00:44:16,720
Bee!

519
00:44:32,720 --> 00:44:34,360
Bay, are you with your dad?

520
00:44:34,800 --> 00:44:36,040
I don’t know where he went.

521
00:45:07,400 --> 00:45:08,360
Thank you

522
00:45:09,960 --> 00:45:11,880
for making me feel at home today.

523
00:45:12,160 --> 00:45:15,040
♪ You’re the only one I’ll ever give a Like ♪

524
00:45:15,040 --> 00:45:17,640
♪ Want, want you to come and be a part of my life ♪

525
00:45:17,680 --> 00:45:20,560
♪ Morning, afternoon, or all night,
I’ll always make you smile ♪

526
00:45:20,600 --> 00:45:23,840
♪ No matter how many seconds pass,
I promise I’ll never make you cry ♪

527
00:45:23,840 --> 00:45:26,400
♪ I’ll hold you tight ♪

528
00:45:26,400 --> 00:45:30,000
♪ Never let you out of my sight ♪

529
00:45:30,280 --> 00:45:32,480
♪ Stay by my side ♪

530
00:45:32,480 --> 00:45:34,720
TODAY, FEBRUARY 20, NATIONAL TEAM TRYOUT

531
00:45:35,120 --> 00:45:36,320
You are so adorable.

532
00:45:36,400 --> 00:45:36,760
Hey!

533
00:45:36,880 --> 00:45:38,120
You should adore me then.

534
00:45:38,160 --> 00:45:39,600
I adore you.

535
00:45:39,840 --> 00:45:41,520
We should’ve started dating when we were eight

536
00:45:41,560 --> 00:45:43,480
so we had more time together before I leave.

537
00:45:43,520 --> 00:45:45,560
You go do what you love over there.

